{"title":"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a prime and both roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337c5774b2276ef05969b4b5e62ea1fb93f6ff17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+px-444p=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"151\" height=\"18\" /> are integers, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b1197e9773b002c10928306f7e85e48f614f116e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1&lt;p\\le 11 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 11&lt;p \\le 21 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 21&lt; p \\le 31 \\\\ \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 31&lt; p\\le 41\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 41&lt; p\\le 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"441\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For integer roots, we need the discriminant, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/141303ccc2054627f5b81ba25a4ab4c1761deaef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-444p) = p^2 + 1776p = p(p+1776)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"371\" height=\"19\" />, to be a perfect square. Now, this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7bea61eda10a882c114ec7dea5c6082699615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + 1776$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />, as if it did not, there would be a lone prime factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and so this expression could not possibly be a perfect square. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7bea61eda10a882c114ec7dea5c6082699615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + 1776$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d36ca737ae45602bcef9dc5409d07686c30bff98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1776 = 2^{4} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e129fbcb9c592946641c11f0c3eb03a078b4bdf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78916550838bd31d66e4cdefbc366edb11fd00bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$37$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />. It is easy to verify that neither <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e129fbcb9c592946641c11f0c3eb03a078b4bdf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5bee8bc4dabea7532e7359aa8ac83217db2f4dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60e1291d8c15e2498c5ea526e003b97dc434e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(p+1776)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> a perfect square, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f250937d9b49e9f657c4a3ce3f9b79543e33793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> does, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de48e93288ea9329c914de4b7188701e04770d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31 &lt; p \\le 41$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bf9089f3c0ad5ee9fca030cfb06b487e559902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{D}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME\" title=\"1987 AHSME\">1987 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1987 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1987 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1